# track/screenshot-analyst scope manifest
#
# MULTI-TRACK PROTOCOL rule 2: a track is a branch plus this file. Every path a
# commit on track/screenshot-analyst touches must match one of the globs below,
# and scripts/qa/locked_paths_gate.mjs fails CI otherwise.
#
# Glob forms: an exact path; a trailing slash for a whole directory; ** for any
# depth and * for one segment. There is no negation in the language, by design,
# so a scope that needs an exception is expressed by naming what is IN rather
# than what is OUT. That shapes several lines below.
#
# Declared by the owner in FS_TRACK_SCREENSHOT_ANALYST_Prompt.md.
#
# This track NEVER writes REVIEW_TRACKER.md. Findings go to the ledger named
# below and the integrator promotes them. That is a rule the manifest can also
# enforce, because REVIEW_TRACKER.md is not in any glob here.

# ── The ledger and the track's own records ──────────────────────────────────
docs/records/screenshots/**

# ── The owner-facing money page, round 3 ────────────────────────────────────
#
# Named explicitly by FS_ANALYST_ROUND3_Prompt.md, assignment A: "write
# docs/records/MONEY_DISPLAY_EXPLAINED.md for the owner". Declared as the exact
# file rather than as `docs/records/**`, because the wider glob would swallow
# `docs/records/reviews/FIX_LIST_2026-07-26.md`, which track/docs-reskin
# declares, and rule 3 requires the manifests to be provably disjoint. No other
# manifest names this path.
docs/records/MONEY_DISPLAY_EXPLAINED.md

# ── Live statistics intake, duty 6 ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# COLLISION, DECLARED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. track/quality-sweep declares
# `reports/qa/**`, which contains this path. The two manifests are therefore
# NOT disjoint and `--check-disjoint` fails the moment a file is committed
# here. Rule 3 says overlap forces SEQUENCE, not a merge policy.
#
# It is not resolvable from inside this track: the owner named this exact path
# for duty 6, so narrowing it here would silently drop an assigned scope, and
# quality-sweep.manifest is another track's file and out of scope for this
# branch. Editing it here would fail the scope check it exists to enforce.
#
# The remediation is one line on main by the integrator, and it is cheap today
# because track/quality-sweep has ZERO commits and has not started: narrow
# `reports/qa/**` to `reports/qa/` minus this subtree by enumerating what that
# track actually writes, or record a sequence decision. See the ledger entry
# SA-013 and the session report for the measured gate output.
reports/qa/live_stats/**

# ── Capture sets, duty 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NARROWED from the brief's `reports/screens/**`, for the disjointness reason
# the sibling manifests already record. track/quality-sweep declares
# `reports/screens/quality-sweep/**`; a bare `reports/screens/**` here would
# swallow it. The narrowing costs this track nothing, because the brief's own
# parenthesis limits it to "new capture sets and catalogue files only, never
# altering existing evidence": a set this track creates is the only thing it
# was ever entitled to write. Existing sets stay readable and unwritable, which
# is what the brief asked for and what the manifest now also enforces.
#
# The set name follows the established `reports/screens/<pass>/` pattern, dated
# as `contrast-2026-07-26/` and `dtt-live-2026-07-26/` already are.
reports/screens/screenshot-analyst-2026-07-26/**
reports/screens/CAPTURE_CATALOGUE_2026-07-26.md

# Round 3, 2026-07-27, added by FS_ANALYST_ROUND3_Prompt.md. Same pattern, new
# date, and disjoint by construction from every other manifest: the only other
# `reports/screens/` claim anywhere is track/quality-sweep's
# `reports/screens/quality-sweep/**`.
reports/screens/screenshot-analyst-2026-07-27/**
reports/screens/CAPTURE_CATALOGUE_2026-07-27.md

# ── This manifest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Narrowed from `docs/records/tracks/` to this track's own two files, for the
# reason recorded in both sibling manifests: the whole directory is claimed by
# nobody precisely so that it can be claimed by everybody's integrator.
docs/records/tracks/screenshot-analyst.manifest

# The brief, saved verbatim per conventions (b) and (f) and per the owner's
# explicit instruction to commit it in BOTH locations with the work. Neither
# path is in any other live manifest, so both are disjoint.
docs/records/tracks/FS_TRACK_SCREENSHOT_ANALYST_Prompt.md
reports/briefs/FS_TRACK_SCREENSHOT_ANALYST_Prompt.md

# Round 3's brief, saved to both locations on the same explicit instruction.
docs/records/tracks/FS_ANALYST_ROUND3_Prompt.md
reports/briefs/FS_ANALYST_ROUND3_Prompt.md

# ── Per-track session report, rule 8 ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Same reason the docs-reskin manifest records: rule 8 requires a track session
# report and convention (a) requires one of every session, but `reports/` is in
# no manifest as the briefs write them, so a track could not write its report.
# A per-track directory is disjoint by construction and makes rule 8's
# "resolve report conflicts by concatenation" mechanical. The integrator
# concatenates these into reports/SESSION_REPORT.md on main.
reports/tracks/screenshot-analyst/
